WEBVTT

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:03.980
If you do us this favor...

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:05.230
I'll let you...

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:07.900
touch me just a little bit.

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:14.780
I-I'll let you have your way with me, too.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:17.030
Want to touch me?

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:18.230
Sure.

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:19.290
Touch me.

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:21.500
No, I can't.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:22.410
Here.

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:23.500
My bass.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.920
You can play it if you want.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.450
<i>O-Of course.</i>

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:31.300
<i>She's talking about her instrument.</i>

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:32.440
What's wrong?

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:34.680
You like it, don't you?

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:45.270
Stare...

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:50.060
Wait, what happens if I touch it?

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:52.780
I'll have you take responsibility.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:54.450
R-Responsibility?

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:56.590
Hurry up.

00:00:56.590 --> 00:01:00.530
Today's song got a lot of views 
on streaming sites, didn't it?

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:05.210
So how hard could it be to fill this church?

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:08.340
That's not the same thing.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:16.160
Your performance was great, but I don't 
know how to gather an audience or anything.

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:21.680
Besides, I don't think anyone 
would come listen to my music.

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:24.060
Th-That's not true!

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:29.300
I-I love your music, Kyo-san.

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:34.650
The melodies are so kind, 
it's like someone's patting my head.

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:37.240
It makes me feel really safe.

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:17.370
Nukui?

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:22.040
Nukui Kyo, right?

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:24.470
You were in my middle school.

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:26.490
Uh...

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:30.560
Toriumi-san?

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:33.260
Toriumi Sakura-san.

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:35.310
You'd forgotten about me?

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:37.520
I haven't forgotten about you.

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:40.780
It's just been a while, you know?

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:44.110
Not that I care.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:50.510
So, what are you doing at a place like this?

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:51.790
Oh, well...

00:03:52.110 --> 00:03:53.150
What?

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:54.800
Something you can't tell me about?

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:56.740
Nothing like that.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:59.300
But, you know...

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:02.050
"You know," huh?

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:06.180
U-Uh...

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:07.940
See you.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:12.020
Hey, Nukui...

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:13.600
Yes?

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:19.360
You might not know, 
but we're in the same class.

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:25.420
Why don't you at least come to class, 
now that you're in high school?

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:28.580
There's almost no one from our middle school.

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:31.020
Really?

00:04:31.690 --> 00:04:34.770
I do think I need to go, but...

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:35.580
But?

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:40.310
Sorry.

00:04:40.310 --> 00:04:42.200
I shouldn't have asked.

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:43.630
It's fine, you can go.

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:46.030
I'm sorry, too.

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:49.260
Okay, goodbye.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:55.600
What was that?

00:04:55.600 --> 00:05:00.230
"I need time to think it over. 
I'll give you an answer tomorrow or so."

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:02.290
It's not his fault.

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:05.690
We were imposing when we asked him.

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:12.870
Suddenly I'm tired as heck.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:22.650
<i>Talking with four people in such a 
short time far exceeds my capacity.</i>

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:23.880
<i>But...</i>

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:44.540
Taking a bath in the afternoon...

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:45.790
There's something wrong with you.

00:05:45.790 --> 00:05:46.740
Sorry.

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:49.010
But how did this happen?

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:51.790
I always take a bath around this time.

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:55.850
It's your fault for not telling me.

00:05:55.850 --> 00:05:57.210
S-Sorry.

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:59.250
I felt like relaxing a bit.

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:00.730
Relaxing?

00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:02.030
You don't even go to school.

00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:04.420
You're relaxing all day.

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:08.500
Man, it's cramped.

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:09.910
Sorry.

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:13.150
<i>Smells like fruit.</i>

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:15.290
<i>Even though she hasn't washed her hair yet.</i>

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:17.480
<i>Why does she smell so nice?</i>

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:20.350
Onii-chan, you had some bad 
thoughts just now, didn't you?

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:22.090
O-Of course not.

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:22.840
Liar.

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:24.110
I'm not lying.

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:24.880
Idiot!

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:25.560
Pervert!

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:26.070
Freak!

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:27.950
Incest!

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:29.570
I'm sorry, I'm sorry!

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:35.080
Little Wing
Orphanage

00:07:05.530 --> 00:07:07.110
K-Kyo-san!

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:12.490
Um....

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:14.800
H-Hi.

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:15.990
Hello.

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:19.500
H-Hello.

00:07:19.950 --> 00:07:21.960
Yeah. Hello.

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:31.720
Thank you for coming back.

00:07:37.480 --> 00:07:39.310
I'm so glad.

00:07:45.050 --> 00:07:45.940
P-Please.

00:07:46.330 --> 00:07:48.790
Everyone's here right now.

00:07:53.330 --> 00:07:54.260
Kyo.

00:07:55.090 --> 00:07:56.950
Welcome, Kyo-nii.

00:07:57.370 --> 00:07:59.120
H-Hello.

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:03.010
You came back without running away.

00:08:03.010 --> 00:08:06.630
I'm expecting a favorable answer, 
since you're here.

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:08.040
Well...

00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:11.790
To be honest, I don't know 
if I can be too useful.

00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:14.070
But I'm happy that you're counting on me.

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:17.140
I'd like to help.

00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:22.060
Isn't that great, Zomi? Ku-chan?

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:25.520
H-Heh, well I'm not surprised.

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:30.020
We're giving him the honor of working for us.

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:36.220
But, I guess, thanks.

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:40.660
Now that that's settled, 
let's start practicing.

00:08:41.810 --> 00:08:42.920
Wait.

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:45.170
I want to ask you something first.

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:49.170
Why did you decide you wanted to 
hold a concert at this church?

00:08:50.770 --> 00:08:54.170
Well, because...

00:08:57.240 --> 00:09:00.180
To make memories.

00:09:13.020 --> 00:09:15.150
It's getting even better.

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:17.620
Your drumming is really solid, Sora-san.

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:18.770
And, Nozomi-san...

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:20.870
Hey, can we stop with that already?

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:24.580
Did I say something to upset you?

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:26.490
No, I mean...

00:09:26.490 --> 00:09:30.020
Calling me "Nozomi-<i>san</i>" all the time

00:09:30.020 --> 00:09:31.440
makes me feel uncomfortable.

00:09:31.910 --> 00:09:33.840
You can just call me Nozomi.

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:40.800
I call you K-Kyo, too, after all.

00:09:42.360 --> 00:09:44.550
Call me Jun, too.

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:48.890
You can call me Kuu.

00:09:48.890 --> 00:09:51.110
Or Sora, if you want.

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:52.360
Up to you.

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:56.790
Uh, all right, Nozomi.

00:09:57.570 --> 00:09:58.730
Jun.

00:09:59.940 --> 00:10:00.840
Sora.

00:10:01.510 --> 00:10:02.910
Well Done

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:09.560
Onii-chan's out, and it's 
still early in the morning.

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:15.960
I thought I'd give him some 
attention since it's a weekend.

00:10:16.680 --> 00:10:20.550
You're such an idiot, Onii-chan!

00:10:31.450 --> 00:10:32.500
That's it.

00:10:32.500 --> 00:10:33.480
Yes.

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:34.980
How about this?

00:10:40.460 --> 00:10:44.080
It sure does wear out your 
hands, practicing properly.

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:48.290
By the way, we need to think about how 
we're going to attract an audience.

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:51.930
I've already thought about that. Don't worry.

00:10:55.710 --> 00:11:00.090
U-Um, the three of us made 
it together yesterday.

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:02.390
Ta-da!

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:02.970
<b>Concert!</b>

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:02.970
<b>Time: Sunday, May 28th 4 PM Start
Location: Little Wing
Guitar: Goto Jun
Bass: Momijidani Nozomi
Drums: Kaneshiro Sora</b>

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:04.590
I see.

00:11:04.590 --> 00:11:06.520
You're going to hand them out at school.

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:10.050
I-I'm not handing them out at school!

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:17.580
Wouldn't it be easier to hand it out 
to people from school and stuff,

00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:19.050
rather than people you don't know?

00:11:19.050 --> 00:11:21.240
S-School?

00:11:22.350 --> 00:11:25.960
I'm too shy for that.

00:11:25.960 --> 00:11:27.330
Well, then...

00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:32.580
It's decided. We're handing 
them out at the station.

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:34.710
All right.

00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:40.170
But I think there needs to be a 
little more information on here.

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:42.470
I don't think it conveys how awesome you are.

00:11:42.810 --> 00:11:45.180
How awesome we are?

00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:51.140
W-We're awesome because we're cute.

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:53.220
S-Sure.

00:11:53.740 --> 00:11:57.360
But I'd like to punch it up a little more.

00:11:57.360 --> 00:11:59.390
Bingo.

00:12:00.940 --> 00:12:02.490
Do you have an idea?

00:12:05.460 --> 00:12:08.580
I'll demonstrate impact.

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:11.280
Kyo-nii, wait here.

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:13.170
Ku-chan?

00:12:13.170 --> 00:12:14.930
What is it?

00:12:14.930 --> 00:12:17.250
W-Wait, Sora.

00:12:24.140 --> 00:12:25.430
Thanks for waiting.

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:26.850
Hey, welcome...

00:12:28.020 --> 00:12:28.900
...back...

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:35.050
Wh-What's going on?

00:12:35.630 --> 00:12:37.850
I'm going for impact.

00:12:37.850 --> 00:12:41.220
Hand out the flyers like this, 
and we'll get a ton of attention.

00:12:41.220 --> 00:12:42.610
That's a forbidden technique.

00:12:42.610 --> 00:12:45.230
How? How so?

00:12:45.230 --> 00:12:48.070
You appeared surprised, too, Kyo-nii.

00:12:48.070 --> 00:12:52.160
Well, yeah, I was, but I'd get in trouble

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:55.960
letting three elementary school 
girls go out in school swimsuits.

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:58.200
It's not the three of us.

00:12:58.200 --> 00:13:00.800
I'm the only one in a swimsuit.

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:03.470
K-Ku-chan.

00:13:04.980 --> 00:13:07.880
You can come in now, Jun-tan.

00:13:14.220 --> 00:13:16.600
This isn't a swimsuit.

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:17.350
Is this okay?

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:19.720
No go.

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:21.750
What's wrong with it?

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:22.610
What?

00:13:23.770 --> 00:13:24.960
Well...

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:28.820
B-Because it's not her normal clothes.

00:13:28.820 --> 00:13:31.740
Let's not bring stuff from school.

00:13:31.740 --> 00:13:36.680
This swimsuit's from school, 
but Jun-tan's isn't.

00:13:36.680 --> 00:13:39.500
She found hers at the flea market.

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:42.380
What possessed you to buy that?

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:44.210
Hey, Sora!

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:48.300
Where did you hide my clothes?

00:13:50.120 --> 00:13:51.720
N-No!

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:54.120
D-Don't look at me, Kyo!

00:13:54.120 --> 00:13:56.770
I see, this could work.

00:13:58.280 --> 00:14:00.730
Y-You pervert!

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:06.360
Sora, is there something unusual 
about Nozomi's cooking apron?

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:07.810
There isn't.

00:14:07.810 --> 00:14:11.410
W-Well, the cooking apron 
itself is normal, but...

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:15.750
See, there's nothing underneath.

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:17.860
Perfectly normal.

00:14:17.860 --> 00:14:21.420
N-Naked cooking apron.

00:14:25.030 --> 00:14:26.260
I'm sorry, I'm sorry!

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:27.660
Forgive me!

00:14:27.660 --> 00:14:28.680
It's not fair.

00:14:29.950 --> 00:14:32.640
It's not fair that you got to see my panties!

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:34.810
You're all taking responsibility 
now, perverts!

00:14:36.430 --> 00:14:38.740
Show us your panties, Jun.

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:42.320
Come on, stop resisting.

00:14:42.320 --> 00:14:44.590
Stop!

00:14:44.590 --> 00:14:46.970
You better not try to run, Sora.

00:14:46.970 --> 00:14:49.030
You're next!

00:14:49.930 --> 00:14:52.530
I'm not wearing panties right now.

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:55.540
Then go put on a pair!

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:57.220
H-Hey...

00:14:57.220 --> 00:14:59.750
You're not getting away!

00:14:58.180 --> 00:14:59.750
Honestly...

00:15:00.460 --> 00:15:02.330
Hey, kids.

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:04.240
I bought you lunch.

00:15:02.480 --> 00:15:03.710
<b>Hanamashi Meats</b>

00:15:20.100 --> 00:15:23.910
Sorry about the kids. It sounds like 
they've been giving you trouble.

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:25.980
N-No, well...

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:28.270
So, Kyo-kun, was it?

00:15:28.270 --> 00:15:29.740
You can call me Kyo.

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:31.870
I'm Sawatari Masayoshi.

00:15:31.870 --> 00:15:33.500
Call me Masayoshi.

00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:36.530
You can call me Master, 
like the kids do, if you want.

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:41.790
By the way, Kyo, there's 
something I want to ask you.

00:15:42.590 --> 00:15:44.830
<i>Is it about what just happened?</i>

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:50.090
Was that <i>TR03</i> instrumental your song?

00:15:51.980 --> 00:15:53.850
It is, why?

00:15:53.850 --> 00:15:55.170
Oh, yeah?

00:15:55.170 --> 00:15:57.850
Jun was right, huh?

00:15:57.850 --> 00:16:00.100
I'm surprised you figured it out, Jun.

00:16:00.510 --> 00:16:02.210
It's nothing.

00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:04.590
It sounded really nice.

00:16:04.590 --> 00:16:08.110
Jun's got superhuman ears.

00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:13.150
She wins right away when we play 
hide-and-seek and she's it.

00:16:13.150 --> 00:16:15.760
She says she can tell where 
we are from our breathing.

00:16:15.760 --> 00:16:16.870
What a freak, right?

00:16:18.090 --> 00:16:18.990
That's awful.

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:22.970
But it's true.

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:25.350
You're awful.

00:16:28.370 --> 00:16:29.660
Here, Jun.

00:16:30.600 --> 00:16:32.030
Here, Ku-chan.

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:34.510
Okay.

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:39.270
Now, then...

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:45.480
Kyo, why don't we have a talk, 
just the two of us?

00:16:54.450 --> 00:16:57.230
<i>He's reporting me, isn't he?</i>

00:16:57.230 --> 00:17:02.090
<i>Dad, Mom, Kurumi, I'm sorry 
I'm such a terrible son.</i>

00:17:04.910 --> 00:17:07.290
<i>The moment of judgment.</i>

00:17:09.570 --> 00:17:11.800
Sorry about them, really.

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:15.800
The kids made a ridiculous 
request, didn't they?

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:18.140
That they want to put on a 
concert here or something.

00:17:19.730 --> 00:17:20.840
Yes.

00:17:20.840 --> 00:17:24.080
They said they wanted to 
bring in a huge audience.

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:25.150
Man.

00:17:25.150 --> 00:17:27.600
You sure are honest and sincere.

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:30.700
Now, where should we begin?

00:17:30.700 --> 00:17:32.570
What do you want to know first?

00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:34.500
Uh...

00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:38.160
Why do you have all those 
amazing instruments?

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:41.500
<i>That's</i> the first thing you ask?

00:17:42.500 --> 00:17:47.870
Sorry this isn't a very interesting 
answer, but I've always liked rock.

00:17:48.510 --> 00:17:51.130
I used to be in a band when I was young, too.

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:55.130
I bought all of it during 
my time at my old job.

00:17:55.570 --> 00:17:56.880
Your old job?

00:17:56.880 --> 00:18:00.900
Get this: I used to be a priest.

00:18:00.900 --> 00:18:03.140
You used to be? So you aren't anymore?

00:18:03.550 --> 00:18:04.460
I'm not.

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:11.400
I've needed a more profitable side job, 
ever since the kids moved in.

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:15.150
So this place is technically a <i>former</i> church.

00:18:15.150 --> 00:18:18.660
Right now, it's an annex 
to Little Wing Orphanage.

00:18:19.010 --> 00:18:23.300
And I've been thinking of letting it go soon.

00:18:23.300 --> 00:18:25.160
The whole orphanage.

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:26.780
Letting it go?

00:18:26.780 --> 00:18:29.420
You're giving up on the orphanage, too?

00:18:30.340 --> 00:18:32.170
I'm not giving up.

00:18:32.170 --> 00:18:36.750
I'll take care of the kids, at least until 
they're independent, even if it kills me.

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:41.940
But we don't have as many kids as we used to.

00:18:41.940 --> 00:18:47.110
The landlord was looking forward 
to making use of this property.

00:18:47.110 --> 00:18:53.360
They're willing to set me up with a cheaper 
and cozier house if I can leave soon.

00:18:53.860 --> 00:18:56.300
So that's my plan.

00:18:56.300 --> 00:18:58.110
At around the beginning of June.

00:18:59.060 --> 00:19:04.030
Is that why the three of them want to hold 
a concert here at the end of May?

00:19:04.600 --> 00:19:07.580
As a show of gratitude towards you?

00:19:08.970 --> 00:19:12.830
I hate to brag, but that's probably it.

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:22.250
Apparently, one time, when I was drunk, 
I said I wanted to impress people during mass.

00:19:22.840 --> 00:19:24.730
They must have taken me seriously.

00:19:24.730 --> 00:19:27.350
When I mentioned moving last year...

00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:31.230
You want to practice playing an instrument?

00:19:32.230 --> 00:19:33.450
We're starting a band.

00:19:33.450 --> 00:19:35.920
You used to be in one, too, right, Master?

00:19:35.920 --> 00:19:37.480
So you can teach us.

00:19:37.480 --> 00:19:39.750
I wouldn't mind.

00:19:39.750 --> 00:19:41.610
But what brought this up?

00:19:44.210 --> 00:19:45.340
Well...

00:19:51.490 --> 00:19:53.500
They're good girls, huh?

00:19:53.500 --> 00:19:56.280
Yeah, they sure are.

00:19:57.410 --> 00:20:01.450
That's why <i>I</i> need to ask 
you a favor this time.

00:20:02.510 --> 00:20:05.550
Can you help them give up?

00:20:07.630 --> 00:20:09.850
I'm supposed to make them give up?

00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:14.330
I mean, realistically, do you 
think it would work well?

00:20:14.330 --> 00:20:16.550
Do you think they could gather an audience?

00:20:16.550 --> 00:20:18.580
I hate to say it like this,

00:20:18.580 --> 00:20:22.380
but they're so lost that they have 
to ask a complete stranger like you.

00:20:23.090 --> 00:20:24.490
Well...

00:20:25.430 --> 00:20:28.090
So I want you to help them give up.

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:30.510
Before they fail and get hurt.

00:20:30.510 --> 00:20:31.700
Let them down gently.

00:20:44.850 --> 00:20:47.960
<i>"Help them give up," huh?</i>

00:20:48.380 --> 00:20:52.560
Of course, I don't expect it to be easy 
to push them away all of a sudden.

00:20:52.990 --> 00:20:55.000
Just find a good occasion and resign.

00:20:55.410 --> 00:20:58.060
I'm really sorry I got you 
caught up in this mess.

00:20:59.290 --> 00:21:01.720
<i>I'm the one who should be sorry.</i>

00:21:01.720 --> 00:21:04.360
<i>I took on something I 
probably could never do.</i>

00:21:04.920 --> 00:21:08.830
<i>It's only going to hurt them 
if it doesn't work out.</i>

00:21:14.850 --> 00:21:15.670
<i>But...</i>

00:21:15.230 --> 00:21:18.960
<b>Want to Do It Together</b>

00:22:57.860 --> 00:22:59.210
It's all right.

00:23:00.310 --> 00:23:03.270
We practiced a lot.

00:23:03.270 --> 00:23:05.400
We'll hand out the flyers.

00:23:05.400 --> 00:23:09.320
Besides, Kyo-nii will help us.

00:23:11.320 --> 00:23:14.830
We must... We must make it work.

00:23:14.830 --> 00:23:20.360
This is our beautiful home, after all.

00:23:25.610 --> 00:23:27.950
Forgive me, Father, for I have sinned.

00:23:25.860 --> 00:23:41.000
<b>#03 The Boy on Hiatus Descends and Flees, 
and the Girls from the church</b>

00:23:27.950 --> 00:23:32.270
Were my bloomers today unacceptable?

00:23:32.680 --> 00:23:36.180
Will I be in trouble with the authorities?

00:23:36.930 --> 00:23:38.950
You will be fine.
